<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<helpItems xmlns:command="http://schemas.microsoft.com/maml/dev/command/2004/10" xmlns:dev="http://schemas.microsoft.com/maml/dev/2004/10" xmlns:maml="http://schemas.microsoft.com/maml/2004/10" schema="maml">
  <command:command>
    <command:details>
      <command:name>embelish.ps1</command:name>
      <maml:description>
        <maml:para>Protects (embelishes) or restores (deembelishes) a folder as encrypted,
base64-encoded text shards backed by a split 7-Zip archive.</maml:para>
      </maml:description>
    </command:details>
    <maml:description>
      <maml:para>Embelish packs a source folder into an AES-256 encrypted, header-encrypted,
multi-volume 7-Zip archive, then stores each volume as a single-line base64
text shard ('&lt;name&gt;.7z.001.txt', '.002.txt', ...). Deembelish reverses the
operation: it base64-decodes the shards back into 7-Zip volumes and extracts
them into a folder. Compression, archive encryption, filename hiding
and volume splitting are delegated to the 7-Zip command-line tool; a
private staging tree beside the destination holds native volumes and extracted files. Validated output is published with recoverable directory renames and retained previous output.</maml:para>
      <maml:para>The encryption password is never accepted on the command line, stored in a
file, placed in an environment variable or written to any log. Instead, the
7-Zip tool prompts for it directly on the console. 7-Zip owns password entry; prompt count depends on the installed build.
The audited Linux 25.01 creation/extraction invocations each prompted once;
Windows console behavior remains unverified. Because of this the
script is interactive by design and is not intended for silent, unattended
scheduling unless a separate provisioned credential mechanism is added.</maml:para>
      <maml:para>Diagnostic events are written as JSON Lines to a per-run file under
%LOCALAPPDATA%\Embelish\logs (or -LogDirectory). The diagnostic file records
operational facts only (operation, sizes, counts, 7-Zip exit code, timing);
it never contains the password.</maml:para>
      <maml:para>Revision 1.1.1 resolves relative log paths from the caller’s PowerShell filesystem location. The script may be installed under scripts/ or in another directory; relative source/destination/explicit executable paths also use the caller’s location. XML help and documentation are optional for execution.</maml:para>
      <maml:para>Revision 1.2.0 implements EB-01 through EB-06: staged archive/restore publication, previous-generation backups, late-collision refusal, canonical contiguous nonempty volumes, exact file selection and diagnostic allowlisting. Native exit 1 now fails operationally. Windows filesystem/ACL/console and managed-endpoint acceptance remain NOT RUN. See docs/embelish/verification.md and operations.md.</maml:para>
    </maml:description>
    <command:syntax>
      <command:syntaxItem>
        <maml:name>embelish.ps1</maml:name>
        <command:parameter required="true" position="named">
          <maml:name>Mode</maml:name>
          <command:parameterValue required="true">String</command:parameterValue>
        </command:parameter>
        <command:parameter required="true" position="named">
          <maml:name>SourcePath</maml:name>
          <command:parameterValue required="true">String</command:parameterValue>
        </command:parameter>
        <command:parameter required="true" position="named">
          <maml:name>DestinationPath</maml:name>
          <command:parameterValue required="true">String</command:parameterValue>
        </command:parameter>
        <command:parameter required="false" position="named">
          <maml:name>VolumeSizeMegabytes</maml:name>
          <command:parameterValue required="true">Int32</command:parameterValue>
        </command:parameter>
        <command:parameter required="false" position="named">
          <maml:name>CompressionLevel</maml:name>
          <command:parameterValue required="true">Int32</command:parameterValue>
        </command:parameter>
        <command:parameter required="false" position="named">
          <maml:name>SevenZipPath</maml:name>
          <command:parameterValue required="true">String</command:parameterValue>
        </command:parameter>
        <command:parameter required="false" position="named">
          <maml:name>ArchiveBaseName</maml:name>
          <command:parameterValue required="true">String</command:parameterValue>
        </command:parameter>
        <command:parameter required="false" position="named">
          <maml:name>LogDirectory</maml:name>
          <command:parameterValue required="true">String</command:parameterValue>
        </command:parameter>
        <command:parameter required="false" position="named">
          <maml:name>Force</maml:name>
        </command:parameter>
      </command:syntaxItem>
    </command:syntax>
    <command:parameters>
      <command:parameter required="true" position="named" pipelineInput="false" globbing="false">
        <maml:name>Mode</maml:name>
        <maml:description>
          <maml:para>Operation to perform: 'Embelish' to protect a folder, 'Deembelish' to
restore one.</maml:para>
        </maml:description>
        <command:parameterValue required="true">String</command:parameterValue>
        <dev:type>
          <maml:name>String</maml:name>
        </dev:type>
      </command:parameter>
      <command:parameter required="true" position="named" pipelineInput="false" globbing="false">
        <maml:name>SourcePath</maml:name>
        <maml:description>
          <maml:para>Embelish: the folder to protect.
Deembelish: the folder that holds the base64 shards, or any one shard file
(a '*.7z.NNN.txt') from the set.</maml:para>
        </maml:description>
        <command:parameterValue required="true">String</command:parameterValue>
        <dev:type>
          <maml:name>String</maml:name>
        </dev:type>
      </command:parameter>
      <command:parameter required="true" position="named" pipelineInput="false" globbing="false">
        <maml:name>DestinationPath</maml:name>
        <maml:description>
          <maml:para>Embelish: the output folder that will receive the base64 text shards.
Deembelish: the output folder that will receive the restored files.</maml:para>
        </maml:description>
        <command:parameterValue required="true">String</command:parameterValue>
        <dev:type>
          <maml:name>String</maml:name>
        </dev:type>
      </command:parameter>
      <command:parameter required="false" position="named" pipelineInput="false" globbing="false">
        <maml:name>VolumeSizeMegabytes</maml:name>
        <maml:description>
          <maml:para>Size of each shard in megabytes for Embelish. Default 10. Ignored by
Deembelish (7-Zip reassembles whatever volume sizes it finds).</maml:para>
        </maml:description>
        <command:parameterValue required="true">Int32</command:parameterValue>
        <dev:type>
          <maml:name>Int32</maml:name>
        </dev:type>
        <dev:defaultValue>10</dev:defaultValue>
      </command:parameter>
      <command:parameter required="false" position="named" pipelineInput="false" globbing="false">
        <maml:name>CompressionLevel</maml:name>
        <maml:description>
          <maml:para>7-Zip compression level 0-9 for Embelish (0 = store, 9 = ultra/maximum).
Default 9 (highest). Ignored by Deembelish.</maml:para>
        </maml:description>
        <command:parameterValue required="true">Int32</command:parameterValue>
        <dev:type>
          <maml:name>Int32</maml:name>
        </dev:type>
        <dev:defaultValue>9</dev:defaultValue>
      </command:parameter>
      <command:parameter required="false" position="named" pipelineInput="false" globbing="false">
        <maml:name>SevenZipPath</maml:name>
        <maml:description>
          <maml:para>Full path to the 7-Zip executable. When omitted the script searches PATH for
7z, 7za, 7zz and 7zr, then the standard Windows install locations.</maml:para>
        </maml:description>
        <command:parameterValue required="true">String</command:parameterValue>
        <dev:type>
          <maml:name>String</maml:name>
        </dev:type>
      </command:parameter>
      <command:parameter required="false" position="named" pipelineInput="false" globbing="false">
        <maml:name>ArchiveBaseName</maml:name>
        <maml:description>
          <maml:para>Base file name used for the Embelish shards. The produced shards are
'&lt;ArchiveBaseName&gt;.7z.001.txt', '.002.txt', and so on. Default 'embelish'.
Allowed characters: letters, digits, dot, dash and underscore.</maml:para>
        </maml:description>
        <command:parameterValue required="true">String</command:parameterValue>
        <dev:type>
          <maml:name>String</maml:name>
        </dev:type>
        <dev:defaultValue>embelish</dev:defaultValue>
      </command:parameter>
      <command:parameter required="false" position="named" pipelineInput="false" globbing="false">
        <maml:name>LogDirectory</maml:name>
        <maml:description>
          <maml:para>Directory for the JSON Lines diagnostic file. Defaults to
%LOCALAPPDATA%\Embelish\logs. Relative values resolve from the caller’s current PowerShell filesystem location.</maml:para>
        </maml:description>
        <command:parameterValue required="true">String</command:parameterValue>
        <dev:type>
          <maml:name>String</maml:name>
        </dev:type>
      </command:parameter>
      <command:parameter required="false" position="named" pipelineInput="false" globbing="false">
        <maml:name>Force</maml:name>
        <maml:description>
          <maml:para>Allow replacement only after successful staging. Embelish replaces the selected archive base and removes its obsolete trailing shards; Deembelish merges restored entries into the existing tree. Unrelated files are retained. The entire previous destination is retained in a sibling backup, reported as BackupPath. Force does not bypass locks, validation or ShouldProcess.</maml:para>
        </maml:description>
        <dev:type>
          <maml:name>SwitchParameter</maml:name>
        </dev:type>
      </command:parameter>
    </command:parameters>
    <command:inputTypes>
      <command:inputType>
        <dev:type>
          <maml:name>None</maml:name>
        </dev:type>
        <maml:description>
          <maml:para>None. This script does not accept pipeline input.</maml:para>
        </maml:description>
      </command:inputType>
    </command:inputTypes>
    <command:returnValues>
      <command:returnValue>
        <dev:type>
          <maml:name>System.Management.Automation.PSCustomObject</maml:name>
        </dev:type>
        <maml:description>
          <maml:para>[pscustomobject] A single summary record describing the completed (or
previewed) operation.</maml:para>
        </maml:description>
      </command:returnValue>
    </command:returnValues>
    <maml:alertSet>
      <maml:alert>
        <maml:para>DOCUMENTATION PACKAGING, 12 OCTOBER 2026
Standalone execution requires no XML, Markdown or agent instruction files. Declared platform/application dependencies and runtime input/configuration still apply. The native .EXTERNALHELP directive is used only for detailed help. Without XML, native help falls back to generated parameter syntax. To retain detailed help, optionally deploy matching script/docs folders so ../docs/embelish/embelish-help.xml is available. Verification text below is historical; current extraction and standalone checks are recorded in docs/embelish/verification.md.</maml:para>
        <maml:para>Exit codes:
  0  Operation completed successfully.
  1  Unexpected or unclassified failure.
  2  Invalid input or configuration (bad arguments, missing source,
     existing output without -Force, 7-Zip command-line error).
  3  Operational, dependency or permission failure (7-Zip not found, 7-Zip
     fatal error, wrong password, I/O or access error).
  4  Reserved for a controlled timeout (not used by this script).</maml:para>
        <maml:para>Scheduled / Task Scheduler note:
  Because 7-Zip prompts for the password on the console, this tool needs an
  interactive session. A classic Task Scheduler "Program/script" action is:
    Program/script: C:\Windows\System32\WindowsPowerShell\v1.0\powershell.exe
    Arguments:      -NoLogo -NoProfile -File "C:\ApprovedTools\embelish.ps1" -Mode Embelish -SourcePath "D:\data" -DestinationPath "E:\vault"
    Start in:       C:\ApprovedTools
  Do not use silent scheduling for this interactive workflow. Append
  -Debug for extra diagnostics. Paths above are illustrative.</maml:para>
        <maml:para>Requirements:
  Windows PowerShell 5.1 or PowerShell 7+, and a 7-Zip executable on the
  target machine (set -SevenZipPath if it is not on PATH).</maml:para>
        <maml:para>Verification (revision 1.1.0):
  Environment used: PowerShell 7.4.6 (Core) on macOS arm64; 7-Zip (7zz)
    26.03. Windows PowerShell 5.1 and Windows 7z.exe were NOT available in
    the development sandbox.
  PASS         - Script parses (PowerShell AST parser, 0 errors).
  PASS         - PSScriptAnalyzer: 0 errors, 0 warnings (settings: default).
  PASS         - Embelish/Deembelish round-trip through this script over a
                 pseudo-terminal (password entered at the 7-Zip prompt);
                 restored tree is byte-identical to the source, including
                 nested directories and Unicode names.
  PASS         - 25 MB source produced three 10 MB base64 '.txt' shards
                 (single-line ASCII); shards base64-decoded back to volumes
                 and reassembled. Deembelish also works when -SourcePath
                 points at a single shard file. No staging left behind.
  PASS         - Maximum compression (-mx=9, the default) applied: 20 MB of
                 repeated text collapsed to a single 8 KB shard. Each staged
                 binary volume is deleted as its shard is written, so the
                 destination holds only '.txt' shards and no temp files
                 remain.
  PASS         - -WhatIf performs no mutation and reports a preview record.
  PASS         - Exit codes: missing source (2), existing shards without
                 -Force (2), no shards found (2), wrong password (3),
                 -Force re-embelish (0).
  NOT RUN      - Windows PowerShell 5.1 runtime behaviour, Windows console
                 password prompt and Task Scheduler execution (no Windows
                 host in the sandbox).
  NOT APPLICABLE - Code signing (performed by the owner at deployment).</maml:para>
        <maml:para>Archive encryption is delegated to 7-Zip; there is no separate authenticity or source-inventory manifest. WhatIf can still initialize/write/prune diagnostics. Staging uses an exclusive sibling lock and fixed recovery directory. Force preserves unrelated bytes and retains the full previous tree in BackupPath/previous. Interrupted publication requires inspection before retry; a rename gap is recoverable, not a multi-directory atomic transaction. Windows staging is private; old access DACLs become protected snapshots, new destinations are private to the invoking user. Unix development requires PowerShell 7.2/.NET 6+. Source/output aliases, linked ancestry and linked output entries are refused. JSON logs omit paths/raw exceptions; native console output and result objects can contain filenames/paths. See docs/embelish/operations.md for storage, permission and recovery details.</maml:para>
      </maml:alert>
    </maml:alertSet>
    <command:examples>
      <command:example>
        <maml:title>Example 1</maml:title>
        <dev:code>.\embelish.ps1 -Mode Embelish -SourcePath C:\data\project -DestinationPath C:\vault\project</dev:code>
        <dev:remarks>
          <maml:para>Prompts for a password and writes encrypted base64 shards
(embelish.7z.001.txt, ...) into C:\vault\project.</maml:para>
        </dev:remarks>
      </command:example>
      <command:example>
        <maml:title>Example 2</maml:title>
        <dev:code>.\embelish.ps1 -Mode Deembelish -SourcePath C:\vault\project -DestinationPath C:\restore\project</dev:code>
        <dev:remarks>
          <maml:para>Reads the base64 shards in C:\vault\project, prompts for the password and
restores the folder into C:\restore\project.</maml:para>
        </dev:remarks>
      </command:example>
      <command:example>
        <maml:title>Example 3</maml:title>
        <dev:code>.\embelish.ps1 -Mode Embelish -SourcePath C:\data\project -DestinationPath C:\vault\project -WhatIf</dev:code>
        <dev:remarks>
          <maml:para>Shows what would happen without creating any archive.</maml:para>
        </dev:remarks>
      </command:example>
    </command:examples>
  </command:command>
